[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4021398360","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117237#issuecomment-4021398360","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117237","id":4021398360,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vsatY","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T06:13:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T06:13:40Z","body":"@mgiuca There was a theme property to change it's color. But now texture and theme color property is removed in favour of styleboxes.\nDefault is now also changed, see the image in the PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116428.\n\nDoes this solves your issue? You can change color via styleboxes.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4021398360/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4021443278","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117237#issuecomment-4021443278","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117237","id":4021443278,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vslrO","user":{"login":"mgiuca","id":228433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODQzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca","html_url":"https://github.com/mgiuca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T06:24:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T06:36:34Z","body":"@syntaxerror247 thanks for pointing that out. Yes that is a much more idiomatic way to change colours than using modulate, you're right.\n\n(I was a bit confused by what you meant by \"via styleboxes\" but yes, there are Theme Overrides available to change the colour of the ring and tip.)\n\n<img width=\"245\" height=\"175\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d2ffd33a-6e8b-4020-ba53-2761a42cd3a2\" />\n\nI would still suggest (while it is possible to make breaking changes \"for free\") that white would be a better default colour for this theme property than black (e.g. label text defaults to white, and I think most developers are going to want the virtual joystick to be white by default instead of black). I think in general for UI elements white is a better default because games are more likely to have almost-pitch-black elements than almost-fully-white elements. So I will leave this open for developers to debate whether white is a better default. (I'll change the name of the issue.)\n\n(Side note: I could not figure out how to properly set these properties via the Theme editor, as opposed to as a Theme Override, since VirtualJoystick did not show up in the Add Type dialog. I'm sure this is a bug because you can manually add it. Filed #117239)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4021443278/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4022483548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117237#issuecomment-4022483548","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117237","id":4022483548,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vwjpc","user":{"login":"Giganzo","id":158825920,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXd9wA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158825920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo","html_url":"https://github.com/Giganzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T09:46:30Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T09:46:30Z","body":"The PR @syntaxerror247 mentioned might have been merged after 4.7.dev2. \nThis is how it looks on v4.7.dev.custom_build [220b0b2f7]:\n\n<img width=\"331\" height=\"202\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fbd9830d-5f7b-41d3-801e-cb7f0019e9d7\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4022483548/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4023326144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117237#issuecomment-4023326144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117237","id":4023326144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vzxXA","user":{"login":"mgiuca","id":228433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyODQzMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca","html_url":"https://github.com/mgiuca","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mgiuca/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T12:13:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T12:13:39Z","body":"I'll have to try it on dev3 later (when it releases) but the fact that the internal implementation uses StyleBox is exposed to users here is pretty confusing. The behaviour in dev2 (my screenshot above) feels perfectly normal as a Godot developer that if I want to set the colour of a control, I go into its Colors section and pick four different colours. Having to edit StyleBoxFlats to specify the colour of a circle is unintuitive to me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4023326144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]